WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.667 --> 00:00:03.267
-Welcome, welcome, welcome to
"The Tonight Show," everybody.

00:00:03.267 --> 00:00:07.801
You're here.
Thank you for watching.

00:00:07.801 --> 00:00:10.567
Well, guys, it seems like
supply-chain issues

00:00:10.567 --> 00:00:12.200
are causing new problems
every day.

00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:14.667
I just read that this holiday
season, there's going to be

00:00:14.667 --> 00:00:18.133
a shortage of both real
and artificial Christmas trees.

00:00:18.133 --> 00:00:21.033
-Ooh.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:21.033 --> 00:00:23.400
-It won't be quite the same when
your family is singing carols

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:24.934
around a coat rack
wrapped in lights.

00:00:24.934 --> 00:00:26.534
[ Laughter ]

00:00:26.534 --> 00:00:28.567
I grew up with an artificial
Christmas tree.

00:00:28.567 --> 00:00:31.067
They're the best. You just open
it up like an umbrella.

00:00:31.067 --> 00:00:33.367
[ Laughter ]
Instant Christmas.

00:00:33.367 --> 00:00:34.601
It smells like the basement.

00:00:34.601 --> 00:00:36.267
[ Laughter ]

00:00:36.267 --> 00:00:37.701
Meanwhile, this is going viral.

00:00:37.701 --> 00:00:40.834
The U.S. Consumer Product
Safety Commission tweeted

00:00:40.834 --> 00:00:43.334
a pretty intense graphic
to remind people

00:00:43.334 --> 00:00:44.734
to water their Christmas trees.

00:00:44.734 --> 00:00:46.100
Take a look at this.

00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:48.934
-Oh!
[ Laughter ]

00:00:48.934 --> 00:00:50.834
-If you thought getting
your kids to go to sleep

00:00:50.834 --> 00:00:52.501
on Christmas Eve was hard
before.

00:00:52.501 --> 00:00:54.701
[ Laughter ]

00:00:54.701 --> 00:00:56.667
It doesn't look like a message
from the Safety Commission.

00:00:56.667 --> 00:00:58.601
It looks like a Christmas album
from Iron Maiden.

00:00:58.601 --> 00:01:00.100
[ Laughter ]

00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:02.767
Yeah, to avoid fires,
water your tree.

00:01:02.767 --> 00:01:04.767
But don't worry about
the long, floppy sock

00:01:04.767 --> 00:01:06.601
you hang directly
over your fireplace.

00:01:06.601 --> 00:01:09.067
[ Laughter ]

00:01:09.067 --> 00:01:10.734
And fill it with coal.
-Yeah.

00:01:10.734 --> 00:01:12.300
[ Laughter ]

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:14.033
-I fill mine with gasoline.
Yeah.

00:01:14.033 --> 00:01:15.434
[ Laughter ]

00:01:15.434 --> 00:01:17.734
Some political news --
Today, President Biden traveled

00:01:17.734 --> 00:01:20.601
to the new General Motors
electric-vehicle factory

00:01:20.601 --> 00:01:23.467
in Detroit to talk about
his infrastructure plan.

00:01:23.467 --> 00:01:26.267
It was Biden's fifth trip
to Michigan as president.

00:01:26.267 --> 00:01:28.701
It may not mean much to you,
but right now, Delaware is like,

00:01:28.701 --> 00:01:30.667
"Who the hell is she?"

00:01:30.667 --> 00:01:34.334
[ Laughter ]

00:01:34.334 --> 00:01:39.300
Well, today, the deer-antler guy
was sentenced to 41 months

00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:42.567
in prison for his role
in the Capitol riot.

00:01:42.567 --> 00:01:48.167
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:48.167 --> 00:01:50.300
Right now, he's trying to use
an antler

00:01:50.300 --> 00:01:51.868
to lift the keys
off a guard's belt.

00:01:51.868 --> 00:01:56.267
[ Laughter ]

00:01:56.267 --> 00:01:59.400
Some news from overseas --
Kim Jong-un just made

00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:01.434
his first public appearance
in more than a month.

00:02:01.434 --> 00:02:03.000
Here he is.
Let's take a look at him.

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:04.334
Wow. Yep.

00:02:04.334 --> 00:02:06.067
Apparently, the original
"Matrix" movie

00:02:06.067 --> 00:02:07.467
was just released
in North Korea.

00:02:07.467 --> 00:02:10.067
[ Laughter ]
-Wow.

00:02:10.067 --> 00:02:11.701
-All the guys walking behind him
are like,

00:02:11.701 --> 00:02:14.100
"Oh, only you could pull that
off. Yeah.

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:15.667
You look great in pleather."

00:02:15.667 --> 00:02:16.868
[ Laughter ]

00:02:16.868 --> 00:02:18.367
It took him 10 seconds
to get into that coat

00:02:18.367 --> 00:02:20.267
and four bottles of baby powder
to get him out.

00:02:20.267 --> 00:02:23.100
[ Laughter ]

00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:25.434
Hey, I saw that Papa John's
is rebranding

00:02:25.434 --> 00:02:27.133
with a new, simplified logo that

00:02:27.133 --> 00:02:29.834
doesn't have the apostrophe
in "John's."

00:02:29.834 --> 00:02:31.000
-Hmm.
-Yeah, here.

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:32.200
Check out the old logo
on the left

00:02:32.200 --> 00:02:33.400
and the new one on the right.

00:02:33.400 --> 00:02:35.000
Look at that. Here.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:37.334
They also removed the word
"pizza" entirely.

00:02:37.334 --> 00:02:41.100
[ Laughter ]

00:02:41.100 --> 00:02:43.801
They said, "Our lawyers told us
we can't call it that anymore."

00:02:43.801 --> 00:02:45.234
[ Laughter ]
-Legally.

00:02:45.234 --> 00:02:46.901
-Can we see the logos again?

00:02:46.901 --> 00:02:48.501
Yeah, honestly,
it's pretty similar.

00:02:48.501 --> 00:02:50.033
And I think that
their new commercial

00:02:50.033 --> 00:02:51.834
is a little confusing.

00:02:51.834 --> 00:02:53.133
Watch this.

00:02:53.133 --> 00:02:54.501
-Here at Papa Johns,

00:02:54.501 --> 00:02:57.067
we're proud to introduce
the all-new Papa Johns.

00:02:57.067 --> 00:03:01.133
You can forget all about Papa
John because this is Papa John.

00:03:01.133 --> 00:03:04.367
So join us at Johns Papas
for some Pizza Johns today.

00:03:04.367 --> 00:03:06.868
Just look for the sign that says
Jopapajama's

00:03:06.868 --> 00:03:09.033
and ask for me, John Jopapajos.

00:03:09.033 --> 00:03:10.968
We'll serve up
some hot Pajo Pajo's

00:03:10.968 --> 00:03:13.434
faster than you can say,
"Snohj Apapa."

00:03:13.434 --> 00:03:15.634
So see you at
Pohnpohn Japajapa's

00:03:15.634 --> 00:03:18.400
under the Papa Jaja Pajpajpaj's
sign.

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:19.968
[ Laughter ]
-What?

00:03:19.968 --> 00:03:23.901
Don't you find that confusing?
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:23.901 --> 00:03:26.801
Right?

00:03:26.801 --> 00:03:29.501
Some more business news --
Apple just announced that

00:03:29.501 --> 00:03:31.767
it's launching
a self-service repair program

00:03:31.767 --> 00:03:35.234
so customers can fix
their iPhones at home.

00:03:35.234 --> 00:03:36.400
[ Cheers ]

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:38.300
Do they really trust us
to fix an iPhone?

00:03:38.300 --> 00:03:39.334
[ Laughter ]

00:03:39.334 --> 00:03:40.834
The only idea we've come up with
so far

00:03:40.834 --> 00:03:42.300
is to stick it in a bag of rice.

00:03:42.300 --> 00:03:44.634
And I don't even know
if that works.

00:03:44.634 --> 00:03:46.100
But Apple will teach you to do

00:03:46.100 --> 00:03:48.000
exactly what they do
in the store --

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:49.501
look at it for 10 seconds
and go,

00:03:49.501 --> 00:03:50.767
"We're going to have
to mail this in."

00:03:50.767 --> 00:03:52.767
[ Laughter ]

00:03:52.767 --> 00:03:54.868
Did you guys see this?
Higgins, you got to see this.

00:03:54.868 --> 00:03:58.701
Mark Zuckerberg just unveiled
the new glove from Meta

00:03:58.701 --> 00:04:01.300
that will allow you
to feel V.R. objects.

00:04:01.300 --> 00:04:02.834
Check this out.

00:04:02.834 --> 00:04:07.133
-Why don't you go ahead and try
taking one of those blocks out?

00:04:07.133 --> 00:04:10.534
There's a more complicated
interaction

00:04:10.534 --> 00:04:11.968
you can do with your hands.

00:04:11.968 --> 00:04:15.167
We can even shake hands.

00:04:15.167 --> 00:04:17.167
[ Laughter ]

00:04:17.167 --> 00:04:19.300
-Finally, the technology
we've all been waiting for --

00:04:19.300 --> 00:04:22.734
virtual Jenga.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:22.734 --> 00:04:24.567
By the way,
I'm sure that's exactly

00:04:24.567 --> 00:04:25.868
what it will be used for.
-Yeah.

00:04:25.868 --> 00:04:27.133
-Rolling dice.

00:04:27.133 --> 00:04:30.133
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:30.133 --> 00:04:31.667
"Don't come in! Don't come in!

00:04:31.667 --> 00:04:34.133
I'm -- I'm playing Jenga!
Don't come in here!"

00:04:34.133 --> 00:04:36.734
[ Laughter ]

00:04:36.734 --> 00:04:37.968
-You're playing a lot of Jenga.

00:04:37.968 --> 00:04:40.968
-I'm playing -- I'm playing Uno.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:40.968 --> 00:04:42.968
-Got a can of paint.
-It's a tournament.

00:04:42.968 --> 00:04:45.267
[ Laughter ]

00:04:45.267 --> 00:04:50.634
-Finally, a stream in Hawaii
that smelled like beer

00:04:50.634 --> 00:04:53.300
turned out to have
a high alcohol content.

00:04:53.300 --> 00:04:55.567
And officials think it's due to
an accidental spill

00:04:55.567 --> 00:04:57.300
from a nearby warehouse.

00:04:57.300 --> 00:05:00.367
It sounds like a miracle Jesus
would perform if he was Irish.

00:05:00.367 --> 00:05:01.801
[ Laughter ]

00:05:01.801 --> 00:05:03.334
[ Irish accent ] "I'm turning
this stream into beer."

00:05:03.334 --> 00:05:04.501
[ Laughter ]

00:05:04.501 --> 00:05:06.467
"Please don't walk on the beer.
Jesus."

00:05:06.467 --> 00:05:08.067
[ Laughter ]

00:05:08.067 --> 00:05:10.601
[ Normal voice ]
Yeah, beer mixed with water,

00:05:10.601 --> 00:05:12.467
or as it's also known,
Coors Light.

